{"type":"finding","severity":"trivial","fileName":"src/state/bootstrap-gaps.ts","codegenInstructions":"Verify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the rest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.\n\nIn @src/state/bootstrap-gaps.ts around lines 51 - 66, Add a brief doc comment above the readOptionalBootstrapGaps function explaining its contract and when to use it vs. readBootstrapGaps: state that readOptionalBootstrapGaps returns a default ledger ({ version: 1, gaps: [] }) when the file is missing and is intended for init or read-only paths where absence is acceptable, whereas readBootstrapGaps should be used after init or in contexts where a missing file is an error; keep the comment short (1-3 sentences) and reference both function names to guide callers.","suggestions":["/**\n * Read bootstrap gaps ledger, returning an empty ledger if the file does not exist.\n * Use during init (before file exists) or read-only operations that gracefully\n * handle missing gaps. For operations that require the file to exist, use\n * readBootstrapGaps() instead.\n */\nexport async function readOptionalBootstrapGaps(\n  repoRoot: string\n): Promise<BootstrapGapLedger> {\n  const paths = getBanditPaths(repoRoot);\n  let content: string;\n  try {\n    content = await readFile(paths.bootstrapGaps, \"utf8\");\n  } catch (error) {\n    if (isMissingPathError(error)) {\n      return { version: 1, gaps: [] };\n    }\n    throw error;\n  }\n\n  return parseBootstrapGapLedger(content);\n}"]}
