{"type":"finding","severity":"major","fileName":"src/state/reviewer-adapters.ts","codegenInstructions":"Verify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the rest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.\n\nIn @src/state/reviewer-adapters.ts around lines 360 - 390, The current dedupe only checks ledger.gaps by ID via alreadyRecorded and skips writes, which leaves terminal (closed) BANDIT-GAP-NO-REVIEWER-CONFIGURED entries closed when reviewers become empty; change the logic so that instead of skipping when a gap with NO_REVIEWER_GAP_ID exists, find that gap in ledger.gaps, and if its status is terminal (e.g., not \"open\"), update that gap's fields (status: \"open\", disposition: \"queued_chore\", source_work_item, source_artifacts, linked_work_item: null, rationale, verification_target: null, next_action) to reopen it, then persist the ledger (use mkdir/writeFile on ledgerPath) and set recorded: true; only skip writes when an existing gap is already open and unchanged. Ensure the code paths that currently use alreadyRecorded, NO_REVIEWER_GAP_ID, ledger.gaps, ledgerPath, mkdir, and writeFile are updated accordingly so reopened gaps are written back and the returned recorded flag reflects the reopen.","suggestions":["  const existingGap = ledger.gaps.find((gap) => gap.id === NO_REVIEWER_GAP_ID);\n  const isTerminalGap =\n    existingGap?.status === \"resolved\" || existingGap?.status === \"replaced\";\n  const shouldRecord = !existingGap || isTerminalGap;\n\n  if (shouldRecord) {\n    const nextGap = {\n      id: NO_REVIEWER_GAP_ID,\n      title: NO_REVIEWER_GAP_TITLE,\n      status: \"open\",\n      disposition: \"queued_chore\",\n      source_work_item: sourceWorkItem,\n      source_artifacts: [\"docs/work/\" + sourceWorkItem + \"/brief.md\"],\n      linked_work_item: null,\n      rationale:\n        \"Profile reviewers were empty, so no adversarial reviewer can satisfy the landing gate.\",\n      verification_target: null,\n      next_action:\n        \"Configure a reviewer adapter or explicitly disposition the no-reviewer gap before landing.\"\n    };\n    if (existingGap) {\n      Object.assign(existingGap, nextGap);\n    } else {\n      ledger.gaps.push(nextGap);\n    }\n\n    await mkdir(path.dirname(ledgerPath), { recursive: true });\n    await writeFile(\n      ledgerPath,\n      `${JSON.stringify(ledger, null, 2)}\\n`,\n      \"utf8\"\n    );\n  }\n\n  return {\n    recorded: shouldRecord,\n    ledgerPath: path.relative(repoRoot, ledgerPath)"]}
{"type":"finding","severity":"trivial","fileName":"test/landing-gates.test.mjs","codegenInstructions":"Verify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the rest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.\n\nIn @test/landing-gates.test.mjs around lines 935 - 957, Add a regression test that verifies terminal ledger entries take precedence over declared no-reviewer gaps: create a new test (e.g., \"land-check respects terminal ledger entry over declared no-reviewer gap\") that mirrors the existing test flow (createInitializedRepo, initGitRepo, commitAll, writeWorkBrief, writeReviewEvidence, writeLandingVerdict) but before running runBandit ensure the ledger contains a terminal entry for \"BANDIT-GAP-NO-REVIEWER-CONFIGURED\" (e.g., a bootstrap-gaps.json or equivalent ledger write marking that gap as \"resolved\" or \"replaced\"); then assert runBandit([... \"land-check\", \"BANDIT-986\"]) exits successfully (result.code === 0) and that stderr does not match the gap string/regex, confirming the terminal ledger entry prevents blocking despite the declared evidence.","suggestions":["test(\"land-check blocks declared no-reviewer gap when the ledger entry is missing\", async () => {\n  const repo = await createInitializedRepo();\n  await rm(path.join(repo, \".bandit/bootstrap-gaps.json\"), { force: true });\n  await initGitRepo(repo);\n  const sourceHead = await commitAll(repo, \"Initial state\");\n  await writeWorkBrief(repo, \"BANDIT-986\", \"Declared No Reviewer Gap Without Ledger\");\n  await writeReviewEvidence(repo, \"BANDIT-986\", {\n    sourceHead,\n    localQwenReplacementEvidence: [\n      \"No reviewer is configured for this repository.\"\n    ],\n    bootstrapGaps: [\"BANDIT-GAP-NO-REVIEWER-CONFIGURED\"]\n  });\n  await writeLandingVerdict(repo, \"BANDIT-986\", { sourceHead });\n\n  const result = await runBandit(repo, [\"land-check\", \"BANDIT-986\"]);\n\n  assert.equal(result.code, 1);\n  assert.match(\n    result.stderr,\n    /No reviewer is configured|BANDIT-GAP-NO-REVIEWER-CONFIGURED/\n  );\n});\n\ntest(\"land-check blocks declared no-reviewer gap even when ledger marks it resolved\", async () => {\n  const repo = await createInitializedRepo();\n  await initGitRepo(repo);\n  const sourceHead = await commitAll(repo, \"Initial state\");\n  await writeWorkBrief(repo, \"BANDIT-987\", \"Resolved Ledger But Declared Gap\");\n  await writeFile(\n    path.join(repo, \".bandit/bootstrap-gaps.json\"),\n    JSON.stringify({\n      version: 1,\n      gaps: [{\n        id: \"BANDIT-GAP-NO-REVIEWER-CONFIGURED\",\n        title: \"No reviewer adapter configured\",\n        status: \"resolved\",\n        disposition: \"resolved\"\n      }]\n    }, null, 2) + \"\\n\",\n    \"utf8\"\n  );\n  await writeReviewEvidence(repo, \"BANDIT-987\", {\n    sourceHead,\n    localQwenReplacementEvidence: [\"No reviewer is configured for this repository.\"],\n    bootstrapGaps: [\"BANDIT-GAP-NO-REVIEWER-CONFIGURED\"]\n  });\n  await writeLandingVerdict(repo, \"BANDIT-987\", { sourceHead });\n\n  const result = await runBandit(repo, [\"land-check\", \"BANDIT-987\"]);\n  assert.equal(result.code, 1);\n});"]}
